**Do not send yet.** The candidate addresses a sourced conflict, but the probe can report “moves” without checking the date the product actually stores—or whether the new question still asks the right thing.

1. **Fix the amount controls.** The tally calls any raw model date in February or March 2027 an annual-filing date. For an annual figure with `expected_publication`, D414 makes code replace that raw date. The control must check the **rendered, code-set date and its basis**, against each topic’s applicable rule; a month match is not enough. [Probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/due-day/dueday_probe.py), [date owner](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:289)

2. **Make sound questions part of the registered decision.** A correct date alone can accompany a changed event, a widened deadline or a faulty rung. Predefine a blind source-backed reading of both arms, including the question, rungs and justified refusals, and make a material new fault prevent “moves.” The promised hand-read should inform the verdict rather than happen after the automatic result.

3. **Protect refusals by topic.** “No more declines overall” can hide a newly unjustified decline offset by a recovered question elsewhere. Compare the matched topics and classify each refusal. Keep uncertain outcomes inconclusive.

4. **Resolve the reading conflict without changing the frozen form.** The audit correctly identifies that the form’s D row still applies the broader filing rule. Report its marks as written and separately record the source-backed diagnostic reading; do not reinterpret the gate to make the candidate pass. [Audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/due-day/audit.md)

The two completion cases are one matter in two forms, so even a successful revised probe remains a small lead. Recheck cost and preflight after the changes.

**CONSENSUS: no, because the probe must check rendered dates, question meaning and matched refusals before its result can justify moving the candidate.**
